{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-25T06:59:50.669Z","data":{"text":"Task 1 complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the blocked-exit and automatic-recertification wording changes across the protocol constants, managed blocks, tests, and docs.\n\n**Core change** (`src/core/foundation/init-blocks.ts`):\n- `EXECUTOR_STEPS[1]` is now the blocked-exit step 2 naming `scope`, `## Blocked`, and `.run/results/<n>.md`.\n- `RESULT_HEADINGS` gained `## Blocked` between `## Outside scope` and `## Next` with its stated purpose.\n- The planner `A file belongs to one task.` bullet now describes automatic recertification, the `osq retry` halt for any other change, and glob re-resolution; the expected-retry line is gone.\n\n**Repository copies refreshed** from the constants: `AGENTS.md`, `.opencode/agent/osq-coder.md`, `PLANNER.md`, `templates/PLANNER.md`. `README.md` adds `blocked` to the wait-for-human reasons and describes self-recertification.\n\n**Tests**: added `tests/executor-planner-wording.test.ts`; updated `managed-blocks` heading list and the `human-steps-guidance` retry assertion; regenerated the three prompt fixtures.\n\n**One deviation**: the new planner bullet reads \"order that later task after the owner\" instead of the task's \"order it after the owner\", because `tests/init-planner.test.ts` (entry, out of scope) asserts the raw Tasks guidance contains `later task after the owner`, and the exact wording would have failed `pnpm verify`. Documented in the result file.\n\n`node --import tsx --test tests/executor-planner-wording.test.ts` passes, and `pnpm verify` (typechecks, build, full suite, lint) passes."}}
